deliberate-differences:
  AGENTS.md keeps host-defined PM/worker/QA roles, the dev/main rule, secret
    custody and conversation-language requirements. The template's role
    definitions and template-wide rule-admission policy do not replace them.
  git.md keeps tasks based on dev, batch promotion to main (#753), and the
    host-namespace prefix interpretation (#623). The author-preservation
    obligation is adapted to task squash merges into dev. The promotion
    merge method is the template's (ddfa4fb46b5479a15748e881130853261b76be51);
    who opens a promotion stays in §Branches, which the template does not
    state, and the §Commits sentence on titles reaching main is dropped
    because §PRs states it. Template
    f92f1f50d9419eb324acfdb56b0ade67d17c8b07 (an agent is not an author) is
    taken with the same adaptation and no other: "the commit that reaches
    the default branch" reads "the commit that reaches `dev`" (#1098).
  documentation.md owns claim evidence and negative-result methods for documents
    and GitHub artifacts, including reviews (#746); review.md keeps review procedure
    without repeating those general rules.
  documentation.md keeps its build/configuration prose scope (#454), the
    issue-completeness rule (#648), and wording about projects beyond this
    one rather than projects consuming this template.
  ci.md keeps the project's prose entry-point description, release separation,
    hooks and same-tag digest-refresh requirement. It does not import a
    placeholder Makefile. Its "Before pushing" bullet states that the
    pipeline runs only for main, so a task bound for dev runs test and build
    locally, and that the hooks leave build to run by hand (#1103).
    Template cccfb36dcb7ddc1242d99760cbf4dd5581bd5d3d is taken (#1095):
    every target whose recipe prints a count names beside it how its set
    was selected. Lint, test and build name the selector ./..., format its
    git ls-files arguments, and build-tools its recipe's tool list.
    §Run the checks before pushing is the template's at
    3d0c87aaf8d363fc304df45a588928febc97097a, which repairs
    bf74ec41bd71df12b93beffb99e81d9e5d44eee6 (#1103).
  review.md keeps the reviewed SHA, conditional local
    substitution and its retirement condition, expanded head-check explanation,
    and the two project-specific Verification examples (#623, #663).
    Template 6ca34218de5fdf40c6776a47c582f32dc04bbc08's bullet on a failure
    naming a cause outside the change sits after the substitution bullets
    rather than directly after "A conclusion is not a verdict", so "the two
    rules above" in the substitution bullet keeps naming the two
    head-commit rules (#1091).
  .github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md keeps the no-empty-fields instruction,
    consultation evidence and the instruction to surface unnamed cases.
    The whole-check entry point and Restructure rejected fields are adopted.
  stack-go.md remains adapted: hand-written test doubles (#623) and project
    verification details. Upstream 37be164190fe985b408fc3b3d095cb4b7321b142
    removed the mandatory interface-named package that this project
    declined (#685); that old objection no longer describes upstream.
    b29f0f104c68b42bfb363351a8e0e3cdc9b52829's heading for Generated mocks
    has no counterpart in this project's Test doubles section, and §Module /
    package boundary drops the template's `mocks/` bullet for the same
    reason (#623). 0b1cf9bcb07c4c0a0c8d4370beac4f44638575ba's
    mockery-location hunk lands in that same section and is not taken with
    it (#1091).
    §Directory layout is the template's as of
    6f3ddf87484bde5c675cb85d387d366bf67a744b, its Service and Library
    layouts and §Project envelope's composition-site exception included,
    and §Module / package boundary's declare/depend and "The import goes
    one way" bullets and §Error handling's adapter example are taken with
    it (#1030). The Layout A/B/C text deferred before it is gone;
